:R-HSA-111463  a            owl:NamedIndividual , obo:GO_0008150 ;
        rdfs:comment        "Second mitochondriaâ€‘derived activator of caspases protein (SMAC, also known as direct IAP binding protein with low pI or DIABLO) in its dimeric form interacts and antagonizes Xâ€‘linked inhibitor of apoptosis protein (XIAP) by concurrently targeting both BIR2 and BIR3 domains of XIAP (Chai J et al. 2000; Liu Z et sl. 2000; Burke SP & Smith JB 2010). XIAP inhibits apoptosis by binding to and inhibiting the effectors caspaseâ€‘3 and â€‘7 and an initiator caspaseâ€‘9 (Deveraux QL et al. 1997; Paulsen M et al. 2008). During apoptosis, SMAC (DIABLO) is released from the mitochondria (Du C et al. 2000). In the cytosol, SMAC binds to XIAP displacing it from caspase:XIAP complexes liberating the active caspases (Wu G et al. 2000; Abhari BA & Davoodi J 2008)." ;
        rdfs:label          "SMAC (DIABLO) binds to IAPs" ;
        dc:contributor      "Reviewed: Matthews, Lisa, 2018-09-25" , "Edited: Shamovsky, Veronica, 2018-11-07" , "GOC:reactome_curators" ;
        dc:date             "2023-06-21" ;
        pav:providedBy      "https://reactome.org" ;
        oboInOwl:hasDbXref  "R-HSA-111463" ;
        skos:narrower       <http://model.geneontology.org/R-HSA-111469/R-HSA-111469> ;
        skos:note           "org.biopax.paxtools.model.level3.Pathway" .

skos:note  a    owl:AnnotationProperty .

